;===========================================================
; VEDIC PITCH ACCENTS (Rigveda) -- combining marks after a vowel
;===========================================================
; Roman-side notation matches the author's IAST keyboard layout:
; https://github.com/oleandrum/macos-iast-keyboard
;
; Reuses [rVow] as LEFT context -- the same single mechanism that
; already drives the bare-consonant-vs-virama and vowel-attachment
; decisions (see CLAUDE.md principle #3) -- so this needs only one rule
; per accent mark, not one per vowel: any accent mark immediately after
; any recognised vowel spelling converts, regardless of which vowel.
;
; Udatta is intentionally NOT marked here: printed Rigveda Samhita
; editions leave it unmarked (it is the default/unmarked tone), and
; U+0951 -- the obvious candidate by Unicode name (DEVANAGARI STRESS
; SIGN UDATTA) -- is in practice the mark used for svarita below.
; See docs/DESIGN.md.
;
; Yajurveda uses a different, larger accent-mark repertoire (its own
; Vedic Extensions codepoints, e.g. U+1CD4-U+1CD9) and is a separate,
; not-yet-implemented phase -- see docs/DESIGN.md.
